      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city grew after the 1870 arrival of the Elizabethtown and Paducah Railroad, turning it into a regional rail hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_City%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1882 the Central Coal & Iron Company began operations, so vital that the town was reincorporated as Central City that year.",
